# Monocular Depth Perception

A Python computer vision project that uses a pretrained MiDaS depth-estimation model to estimate 3D depth from a single 2D image.

The program processes an image, generates a depth map, and uses the depth information to create a 3D point cloud. It can also generate an approximate 3D mesh and rotating visualization.

## Features

* Monocular depth estimation using MiDaS/DPT
* GPU acceleration with PyTorch/CUDA when available
* Image contrast enhancement
* Sketch processing mode
* Depth-map smoothing
* Point-cloud generation and noise filtering
* Optional 3D mesh generation
* 3D visualization
* PLY point-cloud export
* OBJ mesh export
* Rotating GIF visualization

## How It Works

The basic pipeline is:

2D Image
→ Image Processing
→ MiDaS Depth Estimation
→ Depth Map
→ 3D Point Cloud
→ Optional Mesh / Visualization / Export

The system uses a single image, so the resulting depth is relative rather than a precise measurement in meters or feet.

## Requirements

* Python 3
* PyTorch
* OpenCV
* NumPy
* Matplotlib
* Pillow
* SciPy
* scikit-learn
* ImageIO

Install dependencies with:

pip install -r requirements.txt

## Usage

Update the image path in `monocular_depth.py`:

imgPath = "facial_sketch.jpg"

Then run:

python monocular_depth.py

The example configuration uses the DPT Large model and enables contrast enhancement, sketch processing, depth smoothing, mesh generation, and GIF creation.

## Output

The program can generate:

* `point_cloud.ply` - 3D point cloud
* `mesh.obj` - 3D mesh
* `mesh.mtl` - mesh material information
* `animation.gif` - rotating 3D visualization
* `results_visualization.png` - original image, depth map, and point cloud

## Limitations

This project estimates relative depth from a single image and does not produce guaranteed real-world measurements. The 3D reconstruction and mesh are approximate.

## Future Improvements

Possible improvements include:

* Better camera calibration
* Improved 3D reconstruction
* More advanced mesh generation
* Real-time webcam processing
* Interactive 3D visualization
* Multi-image reconstruction
* Object detection and segmentation

## Project Purpose

This project was developed to explore computer vision, machine learning, image processing, and 3D reconstruction using Python.
